    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the order, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (84.24) and **Yordan Alvarez** (82.60). **Junior Caminero** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Sugano; with a park factor boost and an elite xwOBA of 0.373, he is perfectly positioned to anchor our production. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite a neutral park environment, as his 0.476 xwOBA and favorable platoon split make him nearly untouchable in this format. In the high-velocity hunt for stolen bases, **Trea Turner** (70.50) is the tactical pivot of the day; facing a slower delivery from Jake Irvin significantly inflates his theft potential, making him a cornerstone for our SB-weighted roster strategy.\n\nThe decision to bench **Colt Keith** (48.79) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Colt Keith** provided a decent floor, he ultimately lost his spot to the higher offensive ceilings offered by **Josh Smith** and **Kazuma Okamoto**. We are keeping a close watch on the lineup status for **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Christian Yelich**, **Carson Benge**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Kyle Schwarber**; these pending lineups introduce volatility, particularly regarding potential defensive shifts or late-inning platoon substitutions. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Christian Yelich** and **Gary Sanchez** (on the bench), as both draw a difficult assignment against Paul Skenes, whose elite profile creates a significant drag on their individual projected efficiency.",
